{"step_index":2807,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T13:21:08Z","input_tokens":2161,"cache_read_tokens":66732,"output_tokens":2121,"thinking":"Analyzing existing application styling to ensure visual consistency in Phase 9. Identifying the established color palette (page background, card background, and border colors) is essential for adhering to the requirement for visual harmony. The color codes are being documented to guide the implementation of consistent styling.\n\n\nThe current application styling is analyzed for visual consistency, focusing on spacing, padding, and typography to address the user's feedback about interface gaps. Examination includes margins, gaps between elements (metric cards, filters, tables, and the two-column layout), and typography for headings, code blocks, and badges. Specific code block styling requirements are reviewed. Navigation simplicity between topics is the next area to assess.\n\n\nA unified breadcrumb navigation system is needed at the top of the workspace and topic pages to improve navigation. Keyboard shortcuts like `Esc` to close modals and `Ctrl+Enter` to run code/tests should be implemented along with easy problem navigation buttons. Responsive design will be checked: tables on narrow screens should shrink, have horizontal scroll, or display as cards; the workspace should stack into a single column below 1024px; the header nav should wrap; and metric cards' grid should collapse on mobile. Finally, useful empty, loading, and error states need definition.\n\n\nImplementing specific visual feedback for empty states, like search results, notes, practice history, and bookmarks, is needed. Loading indicators will be shown when executing code or running tests. Python errors will provide educational alerts. Test failures should include clear expected vs actual comparisons.\n\nIndicators for problem statuses (solved, attempted, and review) will be implemented as pill badges with specified visual styles.\n\n\nProblem status indicators are required within the problem table, card, detail recommended card, roadmap stage starter cards, and workspace header. Implementation should adhere to specified visual styles for each status (solved, attempted, review, not started, bookmarked). Unnecessary dashboards and excessive animations will be eliminated, prioritizing a clean, focused interface with fast, subtle transitions. Misleading statistics will be avoided by displaying exact numbers, cleanly rounded percentages, and utilizing only real local computer data. Beginner Mode will be implemented with simplified terminology, offering plain-English explanations instead of dense technical details.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/dsa_dashboard.js\"","EndLine":"2490","StartLine":"2420","toolAction":"\"Viewing loadAndVisualizeProblem and updateVisualizerActiveBanner\"","toolSummary":"\"View visualizer bridge methods\""}}]}
{"step_index":2808,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T13:21:29Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-27T18:51:29+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-10-27T18:51:29+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/dsa_dashboard.js`\nTotal Lines: 5166\nTotal Bytes: 244816\nShowing lines 2420 to 2490\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n2420: \r\n2421:     // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n2422:     // INTEGRATION WITH CODE VISUALIZER\r\n2423:     // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n2424:     loadAndVisualizeProblem(id, codeOverride = null) {\r\n2425:       const problem = this.problemsById.get(id);\r\n2426:       if (!problem) return;\r\n2427: \r\n2428:       this.activeVisualizerProblemId = id;\r\n2429:       this.markAttempted(id);\r\n2430: \r\n2431:       const codeToLoad = codeOverride || this.getUserCode(id) || problem.starterCode;\r\n2432: \r\n2433:       if (window.teachMeApp) {\r\n2434:         window.teachMeApp.sourceCode = codeToLoad;\r\n2435:         if (window.teachMeApp.codeTextarea) {\r\n2436:           window.teachMeApp.codeTextarea.value = codeToLoad;\r\n2437:         }\r\n2438:         window.teachMeApp.inputCode = '';\r\n2439:         window.teachMeApp.currentPresetKey = 'custom';\r\n2440:         window.teachMeApp.analyzeAndRun();\r\n2441:       }\r\n2442: \r\n2443:       this.updateVisualizerActiveBanner();\r\n2444:       this.switchView('visualizer');\r\n2445:       if (typeof window !== 'undefined' && typeof window.scrollTo === 'function') {\r\n2446:         window.scrollTo({ top: 0, behavior: 'smooth' });\r\n2447:       }\r\n2448:     }\r\n2449: \r\n2450:     updateVisualizerActiveBanner() {\r\n2451:       if (!this.dsaActiveBanner) return;\r\n2452: \r\n2453:       if (!this.activeVisualizerProblemId) {\r\n2454:         this.dsaActiveBanner.classList.add('hidden');\r\n2455:         return;\r\n2456:       }\r\n2457: \r\n245\n<truncated 33 bytes>\nyId.get(this.activeVisualizerProblemId);\r\n2459:       if (!p) {\r\n2460:         this.dsaActiveBanner.classList.add('hidden');\r\n2461:         return;\r\n2462:       }\r\n2463: \r\n2464:       const isSolved = this.progress.solved.includes(p.id);\r\n2465:       const diffClass = p.difficulty.toLowerCase();\r\n2466: \r\n2467:       this.dsaActiveBanner.classList.remove('hidden');\r\n2468:       this.dsaActiveBanner.innerHTML = `\r\n2469:         <div class=\"dsa-active-banner-inner\">\r\n2470:           <div class=\"dsa-active-info\">\r\n2471:             <span class=\"dsa-active-tag\">📚 Practicing DSA</span>\r\n2472:             <span class=\"dsa-active-title\">\r\n2473:               <strong>#${p.leetcodeNumber} ${this.escapeHTML(p.title)}</strong>\r\n2474:               <span class=\"diff-badge diff-${diffClass}\">${p.difficulty}</span>\r\n2475:               <span class=\"topic-tag\">${this.escapeHTML(p.topic || (p.topics && p.topics[0]) || 'DSA')}</span>\r\n2476:               <span class=\"pattern-tag\">Pattern: ${this.escapeHTML(p.pattern)}</span>\r\n2477:             </span>\r\n2478:           </div>\r\n2479:           <div class=\"dsa-active-actions\">\r\n2480:             ${isSolved \r\n2481:               ? `<span class=\"solved-pill\">✅ Solved</span>` \r\n2482:               : `<button id=\"btnBannerMarkSolved\" class=\"btn-banner-solve\" title=\"Mark this problem as completed\">✓ Mark as Solved</button>`}\r\n2483:             <button id=\"btnBannerOpenWorkspace\" class=\"btn-banner-solve btn-banner-ws\" title=\"Return to Problem Learning Workspace\">🎓 Learning Workspace</button>\r\n2484:             <button id=\"btnBannerBackToDsa\" class=